.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2itwz7_apple-platform-intent-gate/TASK-260715-1o3q6l_compile-gate-a0-primary-source-dossier/README.md:10:1. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome resource lists every primary Apple source with direct URL, access date, relevant requirement in paraphrase, and the architecture behavior it governs. 2. A traceability table covers local HEV TCP termination, SSH direct-tcpip, UDP relay over SSH exec, DNS handling, default routes, endpoint exclusions, and containing-app versus provider ownership. 3. Facts, inferences, unresolved ambiguity, and assumptions are visibly separated. 4. The dossier states why successful local installation is not Gate A0 evidence and enumerates the accepted authoritative evidence routes. 5. Another researcher can reproduce the source review from the recorded references and revision.
.task-board/EPIC-260715-2lz67t_udp-relay-and-degraded-mode/STORY-260715-1nsw9p_udp-forwarding-and-associations/TASK-260715-1ut6ot_add-udp-association-and-datagram-conformance-tests/README.md:4:Build deterministic component and composed harness tests for client associations, HEV translation, framed pumping, relay sockets, IPv4, IPv6, domains, replies, errors, close, expiry, DNS, limits, and repeatable cleanup.
.task-board/EPIC-260715-2lz67t_udp-relay-and-degraded-mode/STORY-260715-1nsw9p_udp-forwarding-and-associations/TASK-260715-1ut6ot_add-udp-association-and-datagram-conformance-tests/README.md:7:In scope: fake HEV streams; fake and loopback SSH channels; controlled UDP echo and DNS fixtures; client and relay registries; all address types; multiple destinations per association where supported; request and response byte integrity; source endpoints; ID lifecycle; PING or PONG coexistence; errors and closes; fake clock expiry; configured boundary limits; cancellation; repeated start and stop. Out of scope: arbitrary malformed-byte fuzzing owned separately, public Internet endpoints, physical Apple devices, long soak, bootstrap installation, path transitions, and performance claims.
.task-board/EPIC-260715-2lz67t_udp-relay-and-degraded-mode/STORY-260715-1nsw9p_udp-forwarding-and-associations/TASK-260715-1ut6ot_add-udp-association-and-datagram-conformance-tests/README.md:10:1. Table tests cover every legal association state and protocol message combination for IPv4, IPv6, domain, empty or maximum payload, source response, error, local close, remote close, expiry, and session loss. 2. Composed tests send concurrent bidirectional datagrams through HEV adapter, client pump, protocol peers, relay sockets, and controlled destinations with byte hashes and association identities intact. 3. DNS fixtures prove priority UDP relay behavior and approved TCP fallback on truncation or relay failure without a physical resolver sentinel hit. 4. Boundary runs admit up to each configured limit, reject the next unit deterministically, preserve control progress, and reconcile frames, associations, sockets, timers, queue bytes, drops, and errors. 5. Repeated fake-clock scenarios return all tasks, channels, associations, descriptors, buffers, timers, resolver work, and counters to documented baseline without sleeps or timing flakes.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2e86nb_m3-physical-validation/TASK-260715-ixevcp_run-final-m3-resilience-performance-matrix/README.md:10:1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix records every protocol field, final configuration, raw artifact reference, automated and physical result, pass, red, or unavailable status, owner, and reproduction command for all required rows. 2. Byte and protocol integrity pass, nominal runs have no ordinary loss, induced pressure remains bounded, routes have no loop or broad bypass, and ordinary DNS or application traffic never falls back outside disclosed platform exceptions. 3. Lane policies meet recorded control and throughput baselines, rekeys survive mixed multi-gigabyte traffic, and memory footprint, peak, queues, windows, sessions, associations, overlap, and pressure actions remain within accepted ceilings without avoidable jetsam. 4. Path, endpoint, NAT64, sleep or wake, captive, relay loss, QUIC, and both route modes publish truthful states, fail promptly where required, restore current generations, and clean resources across repeated cycles. 5. The publication names accepted device and OS baselines, parameter values, statistical thresholds, energy and performance regressions, red or unavailable rows, conditional HEV disposition, follow-up task IDs, and privacy-safe raw evidence locations.
.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-pmww4f_add-relux-tunnel-harness-target/progress.md:40:Developer handoff: added standalone SwiftPM ReluxTunnelHarness plus Core-linked support target, stable smoke registry, versioned and privacy-redacted deterministic JSON, provider-equivalent injection and composition seams, signal cancellation, and LIFO cleanup for files sockets and tasks. Clean swift test passes 12 tests in 2 suites; swift build and product build pass; format shellcheck boundary guard diff check and board validation pass. Standalone smoke exits 0 and usage exits 64. Evidence attached as TASK-260715-pmww4f_results.md. M0 logbook records the macOS sun_path temporary-directory constraint.
