.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2itwz7_apple-platform-intent-gate/TASK-260715-12avq0_author-and-review-a0-disclosure-packet/README.md:7:In scope: containing apps, packet-tunnel providers, HEV local TCP termination, SSH-only user-payload transport, direct-tcpip, exec-based UDP relay, DNS behavior, remote exit ownership, system exceptions, prototype limits, distribution intent, and concrete Apple questions. Out of scope: sending the packet, marketing copy, privacy-policy drafting, production code, and changing behavior to make the disclosure sound safer.
.task-board/EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-l2i2oo_target-project-architecture/TASK-260715-2nfz7w_establish-relux-tunnel-core-and-platform-adapter-boundaries/README.md:10:1. ReluxTunnelCore builds independently of application UI and does not import platform-only frameworks outside explicitly named adapter modules. 2. iOS and macOS providers have thin composition roots that adapt Network Extension lifecycle and packet-flow surfaces to shared contracts. 3. Dependency direction prevents shared core from reaching into containing apps or generated target state. 4. Swift Testing contract tests prove both provider adapters satisfy the same lifecycle and version-message behavior. 5. Package and module documentation maps every contract to a supplied M0 or later specification and avoids implementing future feature semantics.
.task-board/EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-eto58m_vpn-manager-and-extension-lifecycle/TASK-260715-3dv8ea_implement-macos-packet-tunnel-provider-adapter/README.md:7:In scope: startTunnel options decoding, provider configuration reference loading, packetFlow injection, network-settings closure, app-message delegation, stop reason handling, provider error termination, sleep or wake callback safe handling where exposed, privacy-safe logging, and generated macOS target integration from M0. Out of scope: duplicate runtime logic, legacy SwiftPM product changes, system extension redesign, reconnect, UDP relay, Developer ID release, notarization, and app UI.
.task-board/EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-2bfjhn_dns-and-ip-routing/TASK-260715-293sz3_add-route-and-endpoint-exclusion-tests/README.md:7:In scope: settings value golden tests, v4 and v6 endpoints, candidate versus actual endpoint changes, host prefix lengths, no broad exclusions, virtual address collisions, absent family, accepted M0 MTU, tunnel DNS and match domains, platform capability branches, application callback success or failure, packet-read ordering, and diagnostics summaries. Out of scope: live path migration, NAT64 transition, captive portals, fail-closed mode, physical leak capture owned separately, reconnect, general UDP, and private Apple APIs.
