codex
Primary source reveals two important integration constraints: HEV strips the four-byte Darwin family word on ingress without validating it, and classifies every non-IPv4 outbound packet as IPv6. The Swift bridge must therefore validate both directions itself. Also, the external descriptor remains caller-owned; HEV sets it nonblocking but only closes descriptors it opened internally. I’m recording these as contract facts, not assumptions.
