ISSUE #315 [open] SIGABRT in lwIP pbuf_free via tcp_slowtmr on tunnel teardown (Android arm64, v2.15.0)
created=2026-07-07T14:57:26Z updated=2026-07-16T14:58:20Z
### Environment
hev-socks5-tunnel: 2.15.0 (latest release), embedded as the TUN <-> SOCKS5 bridge in an Android VPN app. Android 14 (SDK 34), arm64-v8a. Device: Infinix NOTE 30 (X6833B).

### Symptom
Rare native crash (SIGABRT) inside the bundled lwIP TCP stack. abort() is reached from pbuf_free during tcp_slowtmr -> tcp_pcb_purge.

### Backtrace
```
#00 pc ...5c1a4  libc.so (abort+164)
#01 pc ...35980  libhev-socks5-tunnel.so (pbuf_free+232)
#02 pc ...30b9e4 libhev-socks5-tunnel.so (tcp_pcb_purge+240)
#03 pc ...39968  libhev-socks5-tunnel.so (tcp_slowtmr+944)
#04 pc ...0fee8  libhev-socks5-tunnel.so
#05 pc ...437ec  libhev-socks5-tunnel.so
#06 pc ...437bc  libhev-socks5-tunnel.so (hev_task_execute+16)
```

### Analysis
The abort comes from pbuf_free while tcp_slowtmr purges a PCB, which looks like an lwIP assertion failure, likely a pbuf ref-count reaching 0/negative (double-free / use-after-free of a pbuf on the retransmit/unsent queue). It seems to happen around connection teardown / timeout while the TCP slow timer is still processing PCBs.

### Frequency
Very rare: a single occurrence so far (1 user / 1 event) during normal use, not reproducible on demand.

### Questions
Is this a known pbuf lifetime issue in the tcp_slowtmr path? And is there a recommended teardown ordering from the embedder side (e.g. ensuring the tunnel task is fully stopped before the TUN fd is closed) to avoid the timer touching already-freed PCBs?

Happy to provide a fuller symbolized trace if useful. Thanks for the great library!
url=https://github.com/heiher/hev-socks5-tunnel/issues/315

