   357	void
   358	hev_socks5_set_task_stack_size (int stack_size)
   359	{
   360	    task_stack_size = stack_size;

codex
A critical low-memory anomaly is now source-verified: the README’s `task-stack-size: 24576` example omits `udp-copy-buffer-nums`, whose default is 10. The parser enforces `20480 + max(tcp-buffer-size, 1500 × udp-copy-buffer-nums)`, so that example is silently raised to 35,480 bytes per session, not 24,576. I’ll flag this for the integration tasks without selecting replacement tuning constants.
apply patch
